  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap overflow in the JPEG 2000 output adapter\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-39919.patch: stop the sub-byte-depth loop in\n       process_one_trunk() writing one output byte per column of a sampled\n       component, and reject unsupported bit depths in decode_image(), in\n       base/sjpx_openjpeg.c.\n     - CVE-2026-39919\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: procedure-stream use-after-free and shading overflow\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-101258.patch: copy a local string returned\n       to a global procedure-source filter into global VM, and detect a\n       procedure-sink string reclaimed by restore, in psi/zfproc.c (with the\n       gxalloc.h include and dependency 9.26 needs, psi/ifilter.h,\n       psi/int.mak); require 1-out Functions in shading Function arrays in\n       base/gsshade.c.\n     - CVE-2026-101258\n   * This release also delivers the fixes of +tuxcare.els1 and +tuxcare.els2:\n     - CVE-2019-25059, CVE-2024-46951, CVE-2024-46956, CVE-2026-125396\n     - CVE-2020-27792, CVE-2023-28879, CVE-2024-33871, CVE-2024-46953",
